Reprint without re-deriving unchanged print constants or reading back scanner tables

Every print run called refresh_print_constants: the midgray probe through
the film model (two tc_lut lookups, two density spectra), the preflash
offset, three persistent uploads of the enlarger's spectral constants, and,
with black/white correction on, update_bw_references, which read the three
scanner tables back from the GPU (three more synchronous submits) to
integrate two pixels on the host.

Nothing those steps read can change between two runs of one Pipeline
unless a live delta arrives: every other parameter change rebuilds the
Pipeline (core/params.cpp is_live), and tc_lut_host_ is fixed at build.
apply_live_delta is the only writer of params_ after build, so it now marks
the constants stale, and refresh_print_constants returns early while they
are fresh. The pair path in engine.cpp (apply a layer's live delta, print,
restore) goes through apply_live_delta both ways, so it re-derives as before.

The scanner tables are kept on the host at build as std::vector<float>,
narrowed with the same float(double) conversion upload_persistent_f32 uses,
so update_bw_references integrates exactly the float32 values it used to
read back. The comment that asked for "the already-narrowed float32 tables"
still holds.

Output: byte-identical. The constants are the same values computed from the
same inputs; only how often they are computed changes.


